    "content": [
      {
        "type": "prose",
        "text": "Unified ranked search across components, hooks, docs, templates, and themes."
      },
      {
        "type": "prose",
        "text": "The single \"I'm looking for X\" entry point across every content domain. Matching and scores are keyword + fuzzy (not embeddings). Between score bands results keep the lexical order, whose domain priority can put a weaker component, hook, template, or theme above a stronger doc, and a query that is an entry's exact name answers with that entry first. Inside a band, fixed weights order the matches, so a description match can lead a keyword match in the same band (55–99 holds both). A component's usage guidance (its best practices) is indexed one tier below its description, so the words a reader types still find it. In global mode: with `cwd` outside a project, items from integrations installed next to this CLI package globally are searched too, and theme results name no step that adds a theme to an app; inside a project, only the project's own integrations count. See `astryx docs global` and `astryx docs global/computer-integrations`."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "lang": "ts",
        "code": "search(query: string, options?: SearchOptions): Promise<SearchResponse>"
      },
      {
        "type": "prose",
        "text": "Import it from `@astryxdesign/cli/api`."
      },
      {
        "type": "table",
        "headers": [
          "Parameter",
          "Type",
          "Default",
          "Description"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "`query` (required)",
            "`string`",
            "",
            "Free-text search term."
          ],
          [
            "`options.type`",
            "`'component' | 'hook' | 'doc' | 'template' | 'theme'`",
            "",
            "Restrict results to a single domain."
          ],
          [
            "`options.limit`",
            "`number`",
            "20",
            "Maximum number of results."
          ],
          [
            "`options.cwd`",
            "`string`",
            "",
            "Directory to resolve @astryxdesign/core from: the project's installed Core, else, outside a project or in a project with nothing installed, the Core of the release that answers, installed into the per-user cache first when needed. A docs-only or themes-only search (`type: 'doc'` or `type: 'theme'`) does not need it. A search with no `type` covers the docs and themes alone only when that Core cannot be obtained, and then says so in `meta.partial`."
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "table",
        "headers": [
          "Returns",
          "Description"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "`search`",
            "The query echoed back, `matchCount` (how many candidates matched in total, before `limit`), plus a ranked SearchResultEntry[] bounded by `limit`: each has domain, name, score, reason, description, and follow-up command, plus `import` for components and hooks, `title` for docs, `displayName` and `kind` for templates, and `displayName` for themes. A deprecated component's result also carries `deprecated`, `{replacement, description}` from its doc: the name of the component to use instead and the modernization route. A doc result is the smallest part that answers: one section (with `section`, and a command that reads only it), one docs-tree route, or a topic, whose command lists its sections. `parent` is the command that opens the level above it: the section list of its topic, the namespace a tree node sits in, the topic level (Guides or Foundations) for a flat topic, or the topic list for a top-level namespace. Every doc result also carries `package`, the npm package that authored it (for a section, the package its file came from). A theme result is one theme you can import: `name` is its slug, its command is `astryx theme add <slug>` (outside a project, where there is no app to add it to, `astryx theme eject <slug>`), and `package` is the npm package that ships it (`@astryxdesign/cli` for the CLI's own themes). When a search with no `type` could not obtain @astryxdesign/core, `meta.partial` is `{skipped, reason}`: the domains it skipped (`component`, `hook`, `template`) and why; the results are the docs and themes, and text mode prints one line on standard error."
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "table",
        "headers": [
          "Throws",
          "When"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "`ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT`",
            "the query is empty, --type is unknown, or --limit is not a positive integer"
          ],
          [
            "`ERR_CORE_NOT_FOUND`",
            "@astryxdesign/core cannot be found from the cwd, and `type` names a domain that reads it: `component`, `hook`, or `template`"
          ],
          [
            "`ERR_VERSIONS_UNAVAILABLE`",
            "`type` names a domain that reads @astryxdesign/core, and outside a project, or in a project with nothing installed, the Core of the release that answers cannot be installed into the per-user cache; a search with no `type` answers with `meta.partial` instead"
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "lang": "ts",
        "label": "Find a component",
        "code": "const r = await search('button');"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "lang": "ts",
        "label": "Restrict + limit",
        "code": "await search('data table', {type: 'template', limit: 5});"
      },
      {
        "type": "prose",
        "text": "`astryx search` runs it. Read it with `astryx docs cli/commands/search`."
      }
